Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.
Print your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:
<repaired_code>
<your_repaired_code>
</repaired_code>
<confidence>
<your_confidence_score>
</confidence>
Do not provide any other text or markdown fences.

Here is the problem description:
<problem_description>
One day Greg and his friends were walking in the forest. Overall there were n people walking, including Greg. Soon he found himself in front of a river. The guys immediately decided to get across the river. Luckily, there was a boat by the river bank, just where the guys were standing. We know that the boat can hold people with the total weight of at most k kilograms.Greg immediately took a piece of paper and listed there the weights of all people in his group (including himself). It turned out that each person weights either 50 or 100 kilograms. Now Greg wants to know what minimum number of times the boat needs to cross the river to transport the whole group to the other bank. The boat needs at least one person to navigate it from one bank to the other. As the boat crosses the river, it can have any non-zero number of passengers as long as their total weight doesn't exceed k.Also Greg is wondering, how many ways there are to transport everybody to the other side in the minimum number of boat rides. Two ways are considered distinct if during some ride they have distinct sets of people on the boat.Help Greg with this problem. 
</problem_description>

Here is the Java 8 code you have to repair:
<original_code>
<your_rewritten_code_3>
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;

public class CF295C_ {

    static final int MOD = 1_000_000_007;
    static int[][][] memoMin;
    static int[][][][] memoCount;
    static int budget;
    static int totalFifty, totalHundred;
    static boolean[][][] inProgress;
    static long[][] nCrMemo;

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);
        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);

        int n = in.nextInt();
        budget = in.nextInt();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (in.nextInt() == 50) totalFifty++;
            else totalHundred++;
        }

        setupCombinations();
        setupMinDp();
        int minSteps = computeMinSteps(totalFifty, totalHundred, 0);
        if (minSteps > 100000) {
            System.out.println(-1);
            System.out.println(0);
            return;
        }

        setupCountDp(minSteps);
        System.out.println(minSteps);
        System.out.println(countWays(totalFifty, totalHundred, 0, minSteps));

        out.flush();
        out.close();
    }

    private static void setupCombinations() {
        nCrMemo = new long[100][100];
        for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) Arrays.fill(nCrMemo[i], -1);
    }

    private static void setupMinDp() {
        memoMin = new int[2][51][51];
        inProgress = new boolean[2][51][51];
        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < 51; j++) {
                Arrays.fill(memoMin[i][j], -1);
            }
        }
    }

    private static void setupCountDp(int maxDepth) {
        memoCount = new int[2][51][51][maxDepth + 1];
        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < 51; j++) {
                for (int k = 0; k <= maxDepth; k++) {
                    Arrays.fill(memoCount[i][j][k], -1);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    static int computeMinSteps(int f, int h, int side) {
        if (f + h == 0 && side == 0) return 0;
        if (f == totalFifty && h == totalHundred && side == 1) return 0;

        if (memoMin[side][f][h] != -1) return memoMin[side][f][h];
        if (inProgress[side][f][h]) return 1_000_000_000;
        inProgress[side][f][h] = true;

        int best = 1_000_000_000;
        for (int takeF = 0; takeF <= f; takeF++) {
            for (int takeH = 0; takeH <= h; takeH++) {
                if (takeF + takeH == 0) continue;
                int value = takeF * 50 + takeH * 100;
                if (value > budget) continue;

                best = Math.min(best, 1 + computeMinSteps(totalFifty - f + takeF, totalHundred - h + takeH, side ^ 1));
            }
        }

        return memoMin[side][f][h] = best;
    }

    static int countWays(int f, int h, int side, int stepsLeft) {
        if (stepsLeft < 0) return 0;
        if (f + h == 0 && side == 0) return stepsLeft == 0 ? 1 : 0;
        if (f == totalFifty && h == totalHundred && side == 1) return stepsLeft == 0 ? 1 : 0;
        if (stepsLeft == 0) return 0;

        if (memoCount[side][f][h][stepsLeft] != -1) return memoCount[side][f][h][stepsLeft];

        long total = 0;
        for (int takeF = 0; takeF <= f; takeF++) {
            for (int takeH = 0; takeH <= h; takeH++) {
                if (takeF + takeH == 0) continue;
                int value = takeF * 50 + takeH * 100;
                if (value > budget) continue;

                long comb = (nCr(f, takeF) * nCr(h, takeH)) % MOD;
                int sub = countWays(totalFifty - f + takeF, totalHundred - h + takeH, side ^ 1, stepsLeft - 1);
                total = (total + comb * sub) % MOD;
            }
        }

        return memoCount[side][f][h][stepsLeft] = (int) total;
    }

    static long nCr(int n, int r) {
        if (r > n || r < 0) return 0;
        if (r == 0 || r == n) return 1;
        if (nCrMemo[n][r] != -1) return nCrMemo[n][r];
        if (r > n - r) r = n - r;
        return nCrMemo[n][r] = (nCr(n - 1, r - 1) + nCr(n - 1, r)) % MOD;
    }

    static class Scanner {
        private BufferedReader bufferedReader;
        private StringTokenizer tokenizer;

        public Scanner(InputStream in) {
            bufferedReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(in));
        }

        public Scanner(String fileName) throws FileNotFoundException {
            bufferedReader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(fileName));
        }

        public String next() throws IOException {
            while (tokenizer == null || !tokenizer.hasMoreTokens()) {
                tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(bufferedReader.readLine());
            }
            return tokenizer.nextToken();
        }

        public int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return Integer.parseInt(next());
        }

        public long nextLong() throws IOException {
            return Long.parseLong(next());
        }

        public String nextLine() throws IOException {
            return bufferedReader.readLine();
        }

        public boolean ready() throws IOException {
            return bufferedReader.ready();
        }
    }
}
